# SQL's `IS NULL`: DS0105 with a fix to `isnull(...)`.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where amount is null
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..41
  PIPELINE@0..40
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..40
      IDENT@20..25 "where"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      BIN_EXPR@26..40
        NAME_REF@26..32
          IDENT@26..32 "amount"
        WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
        IDENT@33..35 "is"
        WHITESPACE@35..36 " "
        NULL_KW@36..40 "null"
  WHITESPACE@40..41 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `is null` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:34
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where amount is null
  |                                  ^^^^^^^ this is SQL's null test
  |
  = help: test for null with `isnull(...)`: `isnull(amount)`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | where isnull(amount)
which parses without errors
